# A custom .stow-local-ignore REPLACES stow's built-in default ignore list, so we
# must re-list the defaults we still want alongside our own additions — otherwise
# stow would start symlinking README.md into $HOME. Same reasoning as the
# voice-pipeline package.

# --- our additions ---
# The Swift source is build input; only the compiled mic-in-use belongs in ~/bin.
^/bin/mic-in-use\.swift$

# --- stow's usual defaults, restated ---
^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING
\.gitignore$
\.git$
\.gitmodules$
\.DS_Store$
